)$, in letters $x$ and $y$, where the number of $x$s is equal to the number of $y$s, in the set of monic polynomials of degree $n$ over the ring $\mathbb{Z}[u,u^{-1}]$, for any positive integer $n$. 

  Additionally, we determine the Eulerian idempotent $\mathcal{E}_{(n)}$ for any positive integer $n$, and we express the ring $\mathcal{P}(n)\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}[u]}\mathbb{Z}[u,u^{-1}]$ as a direct sum of isomorphic copies of the ring $\mathbb{Z}[x,y,x^{-1}y]$, where $x$ corresponds to the basis element $x\otimes u$ and $y$ corresponds to the basis element $y\otimes u^{-1}$. 

  Further, we provide the structure of the ring $\mathcal{P}(n)\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}[u]}\mathbb{Z}[u,u^{-1]}$ after applying the Hall basis, and we obtain the expression of the Eulerian idempotent $\mathcal{E}_{(n)}$ as a sum of monic polynomials for any positive integer $n$.
